                <pb facs="0823" n="815" sameAs="frus:frus1940v04/pg815"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102S/2277: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-19T11:00:00+09:00">September 19, 1940—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 19—1:58 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>860. Shanghai defense sectors. I am still withholding action on the Department’s
                    344, September 10, 6 p.m., in accordance with the <pb facs="0824" n="816"
                        xml:id="pg816"/> last sentence of paragraph numbered 8 of my 825, September
                    12, 7 p.m. It seems important to avoid crossing wires with Shanghai if there is
                    any outlook for progress in the negotiations there.</p>
                <p>Sent to the Department. Repeated to Shanghai.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
